## Acceptance criteria for this task

AC-1: `OrderRepository.getById` MUST return `null` for a missing order instead of throwing `NotFoundException`. Callers are being updated to handle null.
AC-2: `OrderRepository.getById` must still return the order unchanged when one exists.

## Changed symbols

`OrderRepository.getById`

## Existing tests that reference those symbols

### T1 — test/data/order_repository_test.dart:12
```dart
test('getById throws NotFoundException when the order is missing', () async {
  when(api.fetch('x')).thenAnswer((_) async => null);
  expect(() => repo.getById('x'), throwsA(isA<NotFoundException>()));
});
```

### T2 — test/data/order_repository_test.dart:20
```dart
test('getById returns the order when it exists', () async {
  when(api.fetch('x')).thenAnswer((_) async => anOrder);
  expect(await repo.getById('x'), anOrder);
});
```

